Subject: [PATCH] fix(world): forward difficulty changes to Bedrock

Translate valid Java 26.3 menu difficulty IDs to Bedrock SetDifficulty.
Retain initial StartGame difficulty and later server-confirmed updates in
the connection's game session. Forwarding a menu request does not change
that retained value before the server confirms it.

Native Bedrock 1.26.60.5/BDS 1.26.60.6 protocol-2225 bread controls refuse
full-hunger use on Normal, consume after a live switch to Peaceful, and
refuse after switching back. Retaining current difficulty lets food
admission observe those transitions instead of a join-only snapshot.

The packet regression verifies Normal/Peaceful/Normal state changes,
the forwarded Java fields, invalid menu input, and the unchanged state
while a valid menu request awaits confirmation.
